netglance is a small daemon that discovers, inventories, and tracks every
device on your LAN. It scans configured CIDRs over ARP (via arp-scan), keeps
a SQLite history of when each MAC was first/last seen and on which IP, and
ships an embedded mobile-friendly web UI on port 8473.

Designed to run on a FreeBSD/OPNsense box: the os-netglance OPNsense plugin
provides a configuration tab and lifecycle integration. It also runs fine
standalone as a systemd service on Linux or as a Docker container.
